  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the maximum probabilities of the lotteries and prefers the one with the lower maximum probability (i.e., the more uncertain one). In this case, that would be Lottery A. However, the individual chooses Lottery B because it is certain and avoids potential loss—precisely because its maximum probability is 100%. The individual values high probability (certainty), which is the opposite of what the decision reason prescribes. The information considered by the individual (certainty, loss avoidance) does not align with the focus of the decision reason (minimizing maximum probability). Furthermore, the individual’s justification is based on risk aversion and security, not on a preference for more evenly distributed probabilities. Therefore, the decision reason was not used and, in fact, the individual acts contrary to what the reason would recommend.",
